WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.937
- This is a really fast,
quickly growing movement

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.873
among millennials,
something like 10%

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.708
identify as a third gender.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.745
So that's a lot of people and
I would be totally on board

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.580 align:start size:88% position:13%
with people identifying
however they want,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.183 align:start position:0%
if it didn't also include things
like medical interventions,

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:20.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
like double mastectomies,
taking testosterone,

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.221
testosterone in a lot of cases.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.889
And in a lot of the cases,

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.792 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think these are
just young gay people

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.861
who are struggling with that.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:30.463
(upbeat music)

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.867 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin, and
this is the Rubin Report

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.869 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
as always guys make
sure you're subscribed

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.737 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
to our YouTube channel
and have clicked

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.906 line:0%
that pesky notification bell.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.575 line:0%
And joining me today
is a neuroscientist

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:46.346
who specializes in gender
sex and sexual orientation,

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.548 align:start size:84% position:16%
as well as the author
of the new book,

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.651
"The End of Gender"
debunking the myths

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:54.754 align:start size:84% position:16%
about sex and identity
in our society.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dr.Debra Soh welcome
back to the Rubin Report.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:00.493
- Hi Dave, thank you
for having me again.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.096 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So I was checking
right before I sat down

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.631
to see when I had you on last

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.733
and it's almost two
years to the day,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.701
it's two years to the week.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:88% position:13%
And we were talking
about much of the stuff

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.772 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you wrote
about in this book,

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:17.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
gender and the whole LGBT
letter conglomeration

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.279 align:start size:84% position:16%
and identity, and
all of these things.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember when we sat
down for the first time

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.916
that a lot of people said,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Oh no, this trans
stuff, this isn't real,

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.720
nobody really cares
about this stuff.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.457
All these things, these
are just made up things

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:33.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
that only academics and
you YouTubers care about."

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.463
Flash forward two years to
where we're at right now

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.931 align:start size:84% position:16%
with your book
coming out this week.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.768
And it's like, this is one
of the biggest issues around.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:45.071
So I guess my first question
is it must feel pretty good

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.239
to not be crazy?

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.443 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- I guess so, but
I've just so horrified

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.845 line:0%
by how everything
has turned out.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:52.812
I mean, I was really hop...

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.147
When I saw you two years ago,

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.682
I remember things were
just starting to pick up

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:58.051 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the mainstream,
and I was still hoping

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.253 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's still a chance maybe
this is gonna get caught,

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.488
people are gonna
figure things out,

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.056 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're gonna be able
to cut this off

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.891
before it gets too crazy,

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.127
but it really has
just gotten worse.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.661
And with "The End of Gender",

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.997
I wrote that book really
with the hope of trying to,

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
again, bring more
attention to these issues

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.401
so that people might
take them seriously

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.370
and realize that we're not just

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.073 align:start position:0%
a bunch of fringe, crazy people
complaining about things,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:22.709 align:start size:97% position:3%
these have real implications
for people's lives,

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:24.244
especially for young people.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:26.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's gonna be really,
really unfortunate

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.914
and ugly in a few years.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.016
- Yeah. All right.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.251 align:start size:81% position:19%
So the book is
really spectacular

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.520
and you dive into
what are considered

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.255 align:start size:97% position:3%
some of the most controversial
topics of the day.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.723 align:start size:88% position:13%
So we're obviously gonna
get to all of that,

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.358
but for anyone watching this,

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.827
that didn't see our
first interview,

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:97% position:3%
can you just do like a quick
two minute sort of recap

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.099
of your bio, of your training

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.967
that led you to write this book.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.404
- Right, so I, when
I was in my PhD...

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.907
So I have a PhD in Sexual
Neuroscience Research,

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.009
I now work as a journalist,

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.478
I write predominantly about
the science of sex and gender

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.647 align:start size:84% position:16%
also about politics
and how politicization

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:04.884 align:start position:0%
of scientific research is really
doing society a disservice.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.819
And I also write a lot
about academic freedom

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.655 align:start size:88% position:13%
because that's becoming
another problem

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.156
that we're seeing.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.991
And so for myself in the
last few years of my PhD,

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.427
I had noticed that
the political climate

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.563
of academia was shifting,

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:19.566
and it was becoming very clear
that there are certain topics

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.067 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you were not
allowed to research,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.036
that you're not allowed
to talk about or discuss,

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.505 align:start size:97% position:3%
even if you are a scientific
expert in the field.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:28.808
And one topic in particular
that I had been following

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:33.279
was the issue of gender
transition in children.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:36.249
And so at that time, every
single mainstream newspaper,

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.851
pretty much I could count them
on maybe one or two fingers,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.486
the number of pieces
that had come out,

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.355
criticizing this at that time,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.624
said that the best way
forward for children

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.092
who are gender dysphoric,

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
so they feel they're more
like the opposite sex

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.762
than the sex that
they were born as,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.498
the best way forward for them
was to socially transition

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.701 align:start size:84% position:16%
at a young age,
younger being better,

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.604 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that once they
detransition, they flourished,

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.672 align:start size:97% position:3%
parents would say that
they're doing so much better,

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
but from a scientific
perspective,

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:04.077 align:start size:88% position:13%
all of the research
literature suggests that

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.378
it's actually better
for these children

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.513 align:start size:81% position:19%
to wait until they
reach puberty,

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:08.982
there's a very, very high chance

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they're going to
outgrow the way they feel,

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.720
they're more likely to grow
up to be gay and adulthood.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.955
And so I wrote an
op-ed about this,

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:18.057 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I waited about six
months because I didn't know

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.792 align:start size:88% position:13%
if I really wanted to
publish it 'cause I knew

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.027
it was going to be..

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.528
There was gonna
be huge backlash.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I asked a number of
my mentors and colleagues,

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.165
what I should do,

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.434
and I remember one of
my mentors said to me,

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
I asked him, should I
wait until I have tenure?

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.972
Because at the time I had
planned to stay in academia

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.108 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I had a whole plan in
terms of what I was gonna do

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.309
in terms of my research,

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.611
and he said that tenure
would not protect me

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.812
in this climate.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.914 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I decided to
publish that piece.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:46.819 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it was a difficult time,
I'm really glad I did it.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.054
And I write in the book about,

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.389
what that process
was like for me

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.657
and what it was
like being mobbed

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.158
really badly for the first time.

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.861
But once you get through your
first mobbing, you're fine,

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:58.064
and they can't stop me now.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:02.902 align:start position:0%
- Yeah, it's funny because I've
been through my own version

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:04.871
of the mob thing and
I feel the same way.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:07.840
Once you get through
it, you will survive.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.810 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's gonna hurt, it's gonna
suck all of that stuff,

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.478 align:start size:88% position:13%
but once you get
through it and survive,

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.380
you will be stronger
on the other side.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.182
Could you just talk
a little bit though

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:20.386
about the reaction
from your colleagues,

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:23.289
because I'm still, I think
a lot of people can't accept

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:26.659
somehow that academia
could be this corrupt,

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:30.396
that when you write a paper
using scientific evidence

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:33.366
saying that when you
transition this young,

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.703
it doesn't necessarily
lead to a happier life

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you use data and
evidence to support that,

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:42.508
that you still get hit
from the other academics.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.043 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like I think people
can't really...

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.578 align:start size:84% position:16%
The average person
who's not in academia,

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:49.115
can't really understand how
that happened to academia.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.218
- Well, I would say
within sex research,

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:54.787
which was my discipline,

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.023
it really has been like a
canary in the coal mine,

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.391
because we saw these issues,

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:00.393 align:start size:88% position:13%
especially left
leaning science denial,

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.628
this has been an issue
for decades in sexology,

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:05.064
which is the scientific
study of sex and gender.

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:07.800 align:start size:84% position:16%
So most of us in
sexology are liberals,

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
I consider myself
still to be a liberal.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think my colleagues
are just focused

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:14.974
on doing good work
as they should be.

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:16.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I wouldn't say, not
that you were saying this,

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.277
but I wouldn't say sex research

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.346 align:start size:84% position:16%
necessarily
themselves are corrupt

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:23.049 align:start size:84% position:16%
and why they stay
silent, it's more that

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.385
they know that they already
have a target on their back.

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:28.421
Usually sexologists are
dealing from science

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.156
now are coming from the
right, 'cause usually

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:32.291
not everyone on the
writers has an issue

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.260
with sex researchers, but
historically it's been more

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.428
on the right.

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:36.896 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now that it's coming
from the left,

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:38.898 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's like sex researchers
don't know how to deal with it

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:41.134 align:start size:97% position:3%
because in a lot of cases
it's people in the same side

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:43.736
as you, and you're you
feel as though, well,

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.338 align:start size:88% position:13%
is this really as
important as calling out

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:46.839
when the right comes after us?

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.841
So I think that's
one layer of it.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.810 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know it's very
competitive in academia

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:54.347
and to get a tenure position
is almost unheard of nowadays.

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:57.150 align:start size:84% position:16%
So you're very busy,
it's stressful.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.085 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then you have
these other academics

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:01.821
and other disciplines
who are not scientific,

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.956 align:start size:88% position:13%
not to say that they
all have bad intentions,

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:07.260
but they're starting to take
over, they're the most vocal.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.895
And they're getting a
lot of support also,

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:11.464 align:start size:88% position:13%
I would say by
mainstream news outlets.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.433
So as time goes on, it feels,

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:17.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think more and more
like you have more to lose

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.471
than to gain by speaking out,

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:20.339
so why start speaking out now?

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:22.742 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's how we
got to where we are.

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:24.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
- So one of the things
that I'm really amazed by,

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.979
and I've brought this
up with a couple guests

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.981 align:start size:84% position:16%
when I've talked
about the trans issue,

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.783 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've talked about this
with Douglas Murray

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:33.019
and with Rob Smith and
a couple of other people

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:35.922
is that in many ways
the trans movement now

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:40.793 align:start size:84% position:16%
seems almost
perversely anti-gay,

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:43.930
meaning that if you're
in a feminine young boy,

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:48.501
they would rather see you
transitioned to be female,

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:52.538
rather than accept that you
actually are just a gay male.

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:54.841
So I also think just
for me personally,

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:57.443 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's particularly
weird because I played

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:58.945
with "G.I. Joe and
the Transformers".

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:01.981 align:start size:84% position:16%
So no one thought I
was gay per se, right?

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.216
But if I...

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:04.851
But I have friends that
played that were boys

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:06.786
that played with Barbies and
people thought they were gay

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.387
when they were five.

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:09.922
And that if they now,

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
even though they're maybe
in their forties now,

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:14.760
if they were growing up now
and they were four years old,

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.062
five years old doing that,

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:18.564
they would have been
put through transition.

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:22.168
And that seems sort of
anti-gay, doesn't it?

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:26.305
- 100%, 100% and myself,
as we talked last time

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:28.708
I was with you, I grew
up in the gay community.

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.209
I find this very upsetting.

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:32.178
I have countless friends
who have reached out to me

00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.013 align:start size:84% position:16%
over the years saying,
you know, "Deborah,

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.214
if I were growing up now,

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:36.649
I probably would
have transitioned."

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:38.117 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because this is
such a common thing,

00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:42.188 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you are a young child
who is likely going to grow up

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:44.624
to be gay, you tend
to be gender atypical

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:46.459 align:start size:88% position:13%
and have interests that
are gender atypical

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:48.528
and friends of the opposite sex.

00:08:48.528 --> 00:08:51.197 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that's been a
huge concern of mine,

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:54.400 align:start size:97% position:3%
especially we talked also
about how transitioning now,

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.968
I consider it, and I
think many in the field

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:59.205
will agree, that it is like
the new conversion therapy,

00:08:59.205 --> 00:09:03.342
where if you have
healthy gay child,

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:05.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
say you have a little
boy, who's very feminine,

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:07.480 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think some
parents have a sense

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.348
there's a chance that he's
gonna grow up to be gay.

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:12.451
So if he's attracted to
men, when he's older,

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:15.254
if he transitions to female
as a child, when he grows up,

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:18.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's going to be or appear
to be a straight woman.

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:19.392
So that, I mean...

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:21.794 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think homophobia
does play a role

00:09:21.794 --> 00:09:23.062
in terms of the parents who...

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:24.764
Not for all of them,
but for some of them

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:26.098
who are so on board with this

00:09:26.098 --> 00:09:27.600 align:start size:88% position:13%
and who are championing
this movement.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.335 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then there's
another layer I think

00:09:29.335 --> 00:09:33.072 align:start size:97% position:3%
