00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:14.940 align:start size:97% position:3%
or because it is easier to
not identify as gay in society

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.842
because there is
still homophobia.

00:11:16.842 --> 00:11:18.077
And so again-

00:11:18.077 --> 00:11:19.378 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Can you just explain
what non-binary is,

00:11:19.378 --> 00:11:21.981 align:start size:84% position:16%
just for someone
that might not know?

00:11:21.981 --> 00:11:25.951
- Yeah, so it's people who
identify as third gender.

00:11:25.951 --> 00:11:28.487
So they may say they're
both genders or neither.

00:11:28.487 --> 00:11:32.425
And so non-binary gender
fluid, gender neutral,

00:11:32.425 --> 00:11:34.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
gender queer, even though
queer is considered

00:11:34.126 --> 00:11:36.929
by some peoples to be a
slur against gay people,

00:11:36.929 --> 00:11:39.065
I don't tend to like
to use the word queer.

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:43.169
So yeah, so this
is a really fast,

00:11:43.169 --> 00:11:46.972 align:start size:88% position:13%
quickly growing movement
among millennials.

00:11:46.972 --> 00:11:49.775 align:start size:97% position:3%
Something like 10%
identify as a third gender.

00:11:49.775 --> 00:11:53.245
So that's a lot of people and
I would be totally on board

00:11:53.245 --> 00:11:54.747
people identifying
however they want.

00:11:54.747 --> 00:11:58.250 align:start position:0%
If it didn't also include things
like medical interventions,

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:01.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
like double mastectomies,
taking testosterone,

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:02.188
testosterone, a lot of cases.

00:12:02.188 --> 00:12:03.856
And in a lot of the cases,

00:12:03.856 --> 00:12:06.726 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think these are
just young gay people

00:12:06.726 --> 00:12:08.828
who are struggling with that

00:12:08.828 --> 00:12:10.496
and we should offer them support

00:12:10.496 --> 00:12:14.066 align:start size:97% position:3%
instead of having them
undergo these interventions.

00:12:14.066 --> 00:12:15.735
- Right? So that's what
I think is so interesting

00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:17.703 align:start size:88% position:13%
about this, because I
think the average person

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:20.106
wants most people to
live and let live.

00:12:20.106 --> 00:12:22.108 align:start size:84% position:16%
However you identify,
that's fine,

00:12:22.108 --> 00:12:25.144 align:start size:97% position:3%
as long as you're not forcing
someone to do something,

00:12:25.144 --> 00:12:27.813
I think what, what happens
then is this next version

00:12:27.813 --> 00:12:30.516
where it's like you can
say you're non-binary,

00:12:30.516 --> 00:12:32.952
